description: STAGE 1 - Strict extraction rules and intermediate schema (internal use only, never printed)
alwaysApply: true
---

STRICT EXTRACTION RULES:
- supplier_name is the invoice issuer/service provider; bill_to_name is the customer/account holder.
- A prominent logo or brand name is strong supplier evidence.
- Do not treat the first visible company/address block as the supplier without checking its role.
- Extract only values explicitly visible or clearly labeled.
- If a field is not shown, return null.
- Do not assume quantity = 1.
- Do not invent UOM values such as "service", "each", or "unit".
- Do not copy the line amount into price unless it is explicitly labeled as price/rate.
- Preserve item descriptions exactly as printed; do not expand or rewrite them.
- For a single visible service charge, create one line item with only the visible description and amount; keep quantity, units, and price null unless explicitly shown.
- Map "Please pay by", "Due date", or "Payment due" to due_date, not payment_terms.
- Use the STAGE 1 intermediate schema below.
- If a field is missing for a line item or header, use null.
- Do not invent fields.
- Do not add any header or shipment data to any line item.

